<para id="RM00000207V004X" category="J" type-id="800XU" name-id="950V0-00" from="200612">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>Main Body ECU Communication Stop Mode</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM00000207V004X_01" type-id="33" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00000DI00000">
<name>Function Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.42in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.83in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.83in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Diagnosis Item</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Symptom</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Suspected Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Main Body ECU Communication Stop Mode</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>"Main Body" is not displayed on the "CAN Bus Connected ECU Check" screen of TaSCAN</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Corresponds to "Main Body ECU Communication Stop Mode" in the DTC combination table</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Instrument panel junction block assembly (main body ECU) branch line open or connector</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Instrument panel junction block assembly (main body ECU) power source system</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Instrument panel junction block assembly (main body ECU) internal malfunction</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000207V004X_02" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00000DJ00000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B162440J02" width="7.106578999in" height="5.787629434in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000207V004X_03" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___00000DK00000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten3>
<ptxt>When measuring the resistance of the CAN bus, turn the ignition switch off, check that warning functions such as the key reminder warning system are not operating, and leave the vehicle for at least 1 minutes without operating the key or switches or opening and closing the doors before starting the measurement. If it is necessary to open a door during inspection, open it beforehand.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When inspecting each connector, before disconnecting it, push the connector case in the connecting direction and check that the connector is not loose or disconnected.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When disconnecting a connector, check that the connector terminals and connector case are free of damage, deformation, corrosion, etc.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000207V004X_04" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM00000207V004X_04_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___00000DL00000">
<testtitle>CAN Bus Open Circuit Inspection (Main Body ECU Branch Line)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn the IG OFF and disconnect vehicle harness connector A of the instrument panel junction block assembly (main body ECU).</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Measure the resistance between the terminals of the vehicle harness connector of the main body ECU (vehicle front side).</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C129972J05" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.89in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.11in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.13in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>A19(CANH) - A18(CANL)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>IG OFF</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>54 to 69Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000207V004X_04_0002" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000207V004X_04_0004" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000207V004X_04_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___00000DM00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness (ECU Power Source System)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect connectors B and E of the instrument panel junction block assembly (main body ECU).</ptxt>
</test1>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="G100284J08" width="2.775699831in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), inspect the resistance and voltage between each terminal of the vehicle side wire harness connector and body ground.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.88in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.09in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.16in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>E17 (GND1) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
<table>
<title>Voltage</title>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.86in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.10in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.17in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>B1 (B) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>11 to 14V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>B24 (IG) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>IG ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>11 to 14V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000207V004X_04_0003" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000207V004X_04_0005" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
